# HTTP proxy for CLI

When running **pip**, **curl**, **wget**, **npm**, **git clone/fetch** (if needed), or any other command that downloads from the network in this project, always route traffic through:

- `http://10.158.100.9:8080`

## PowerShell (preferred on Windows)

Set before the command (or in the same shell invocation):

```powershell
$env:HTTP_PROXY="http://10.158.100.9:8080"
$env:HTTPS_PROXY="http://10.158.100.9:8080"
$env:http_proxy="http://10.158.100.9:8080"
$env:https_proxy="http://10.158.100.9:8080"
```

## Examples

```powershell
pip install -r requirements.txt
curl -x http://10.158.100.9:8080 https://example.com
```

For pip you may also use: `pip install --proxy http://10.158.100.9:8080 ...`

Do not omit the proxy for install/download commands unless the user explicitly says to run offline or without proxy.
